THE SINGLE DEFECT AND ITS FIX
  L777 `theorem h1_same_repair_different_probe_not_congruent ... := by decide`
  error: failed to synthesize Decidable ((∀ a, f2R .u1 a = f2R .u2 a) ∧
         minimaxV ... [.u1, .v] = .fin 2 ∧ minimaxV ... [.u2, .v] = .inf)
  Cause: `decide` cannot synthesise a Decidable instance for a conjunction whose
  components mix a bounded ∀ over AtomAction with two minimaxV equals-cost tests;
  instance search does not unfold minimaxV far enough inside a nested ∧.
  Fix (statements unchanged, theorem keeps the identical type): split into three
  separately-decided parts and assemble the conjunction from them:
    h1_part_repr : ∀ a, f2R .u1 a = f2R .u2 a                 (by intro a; cases a <;> rfl)
    h1_part_u1   : minimaxV ... [.u1, .v] = .fin 2             (by decide)
    h1_part_u2   : minimaxV ... [.u2, .v] = .inf               (by decide)
    h1_same_... : <original conjunction> := ⟨h1_part_repr, h1_part_u1, h1_part_u2⟩

WHAT v1.3 ADDS (four new results, all now genuinely proved)
  adaptive_strictly_beats_nonadaptive        [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]
