  h1_same_repair_different_probe_not_congruent [propext]   (was [propext, sorryAx])
  unaffordable_probe_irrelevant              [propext]
  These are exactly the operational-congruence facts: h=0 collapses to the repair
  profile (dominated worlds are redundant), while h>=1 separates worlds with equal
  repair profiles because the probe splits them, and the (h, B) cutoff makes
  unaffordable probes irrelevant. The parametrisation by B is now machine-checked,
  not just asserted in prose.

